      "narrative": null,
      "content": "LLM-Based Multi-Agent Systems for Software Engineering:\nLiterature Review, Vision and the Road Ahead\nJUNDA HE, Singapore Management University, Singapore\nCHRISTOPH TREUDE, Singapore Management University, Singapore\nDAVID LO, Singapore Management University, Singapore\nIntegrating Large Language Models (LLMs) into autonomous agents marks a significant shift in the research\nlandscape by offering cognitive abilities that are competitive with human planning and reasoning. This\npaper explores the transformative potential of integrating Large Language Models into Multi-Agent (LMA)\nsystems for address",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Title, authors and abstract of \"LLM-Based Multi-Agent Systems for Software Engineering: Literature Review, Vision and the Road Ahead\" by Junda He, Christoph Treude and David Lo (Singapore Management University). LLM-based multi-agent (LMA) systems use the collaborative, specialised abilities of several agents for autonomous problem-solving, robustness and scalability in software engineering. The paper systematically reviews recent primary studies of LMA applications across the software development lifecycle, runs two case studies of a state-of-the-art LMA framework, and proposes a research agenda on enhancing individual agents and optimising their synergy, toward what it calls Software Engineering 2.0.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
