      "narrative": null,
      "content": "2.1\nAutonomous Agent\nAn autonomous agent is a computational entity designed for independent and effective operation\nin dynamic environments [98]. Its essential attributes are:\n• Autonomy: Independently manages its actions and internal state without external controls.\n• Perception: Detects the changes in the surrounding environment through sensory mechanisms.\n• Intelligence and Goal-Driven: Aims for specific goals using domain-specific knowledge and\nproblem-solving abilities.\n• Social Ability: Can interact with humans or other agents, manages social relationships to\nachieve goals.\n• Learning Ca",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Preliminaries on autonomous agents: a computational entity operating independently in dynamic environments, with the attributes of autonomy, perception, intelligence and goal-direction, social ability, and learning.",
