      "target": "../sections/sec-005-22-llm-based-autonomous-agent.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Formally speaking, an LLM-based agent can be described by the tuple ⟨𝐿,𝑂, 𝑀, 𝑃,𝐴, 𝑅⟩[24], where:\n• 𝐿symbolizes the Large Language Model, serving as the agent’s cognitive core. It is equipped\nwith extensive knowledge, potentially fine-tuned for specific domains, allowing it to make\ninformed decisions based on observations, feedback, and rewards. Typically, an LLM suited for\nthis role is trained on vast corpora of diverse textual data and comprises billions of parameters,\nsuch as models like ChatGPT1, Claude2, and Gemini3. These models exhibit strong zero-shot and\nfew-shot learning capabi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "LLM-based agents, LMA systems and the review's search strategy. An LLM-based agent is the tuple ⟨L, O, M, P, A, R⟩: the LLM as cognitive core, the objective, memory, perception, action (tool use and communication) and rethink, a reflective step after acting. An LMA system has an orchestration platform, which sets coordination models (cooperative, competitive, hierarchical or mixed), communication mechanisms (centralised, decentralised or hierarchical, exchanging artefacts such as code, commit messages or bug reports) and planning styles (centralised or decentralised planning with decentralised execution), plus agents that are predefined or generated, homogeneous or heterogeneous, viewed as nodes of an interaction graph. The review searched DBLP paper titles with agent keywords (Agent, LLM, Large Language Model, Collaborat) combined with truncated phase-specific SE keywords.",
