      "narrative": null,
      "content": "To demonstrate the practical effectiveness of LMA systems, we conduct two case studies. Specif-\nically, we utilize the state-of-the-art LMA framework, ChatDev [109], to autonomously develop\ntwo classic games: Snake and Tetris. ChatDev structures the software development process into\nthree phases: designing, coding, and testing. ChatDev employs specialized roles, including CEO,\nCTO, programmer, reviewer, and tester. ChatDev’s agents are powered by GPT-3.5-turbo4. The\ntemperature setting controls the randomness and creativity of the GPT-3.5’s responses. Following\nthe original ChatDev setting, we",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The case-study setup: the authors use ChatDev, whose CEO, CTO, programmer, reviewer and tester agents work through designing, coding and testing phases on GPT-3.5-turbo at temperature 0.2, to build two classic games, Snake and Tetris.",
